1. Introduction

1.1 Purpose

This document specifies the requirements for Foresight Android — a local-first, multimodal AI assistant for Android, modeled on Google AI Edge Foresight. The SRS is written in conformance with ISO/IEC/IEEE 29148:2018 and defines requirements that are necessary, unambiguous, verifiable, feasible, and singular .

1.2 Scope

Foresight Android will:

· Capture live meeting audio and index notes, documents, and media on-device.
· Build a unified multimodal memory graph using EmbeddingGemma 2 embeddings.
· Provide semantic search and local LLM-generated answers (Gemma 4 via LiteRT-LM).
· Expose an MCP client bridge to s-ai-swarm, zoe-mcp, and glama-gateway.
· Offer optional Google Sign-In for identity and per-user profile partitioning.
· Ship as a signed APK built through an agent-assisted, skill-grounded pipeline using Google's android/skills.

Out of scope for v1.0: cloud sync, iOS, multi-user collaboration, wearable/XR extensions.

1.3 Intended Audience

· Developer: Sai Karun Nandipati — architecture, agent orchestration, validation.
· Research reviewers: Agentic AI / on-device ML.
· JOSS reviewers: Open-source publication track.
· End user: Privacy-conscious Android users.

