2. Product Overview

2.1 Product Perspective

Foresight Android is a standalone Android application sharing architectural DNA with the karun99 portfolio. Its build pipeline is agent-driven and skill-grounded, and its runtime is local-first with optional identity.

```
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                  Agent-Driven Build Loop                     │
│                                                              │
│   android/skills  ──►  Agent  ──►  APK  ──►  neural-harness  │
│   (SKILL.md)          (code)      (output)   (validation)    │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                    Android Application                       │
│                                                              │
│  Capture → Embedding → Memory Graph → Local LLM → MCP Bridge │
│                                                              │
│  ┌────────────────┐                                          │
│  │ Google Sign-In │──► Per-user memory graph partitioning    │
│  │   (optional)   │──► Server auth code → future desktop sync│
│  └────────────────┘                                          │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

2.2 Product Functions (High-Level)

· F1 Live meeting capture (on-device ASR).
· F2 Multimodal indexing (text, image, audio, video).
· F3 Semantic search over the memory graph.
· F4 Local summarization and Q&A.
· F5 MCP tool invocation via stdio/localhost bridge.
· F6 Consent-gated recording.
· F7 Zero-network mode (airplane-mode full function).
· F8 Agent-assisted, skill-grounded build.
· F9 Optional Google Sign-In for identity and profile partitioning.

2.3 User Characteristics

· Privacy-conscious professional or researcher.
· Expects sub-second query response after indexing.
· May not be technical; UI hides model internals.
· May use a shared device with multiple profiles.

