3.3 External Interface Requirements

3.3.1 User Interfaces

· Recording screen: waveform, live transcript, note field.
· Search screen: query bar, filter chips, result cards.
· Answer screen: summary + cited chunks.
· Settings: model selection, k, temperature, consent tiers, MCP endpoints, sign-out/revoke.
· Trust dashboard: TRL badge, VISION marker, skill-compliance score, last validation run.

3.3.2 Hardware Interfaces

· Microphone (RECORD_AUDIO).
· NNAPI / GPU delegate (optional acceleration).
· Storage (app-private + optional SAF for imports).

3.3.3 Software Interfaces

· LiteRT-LM for model runtime (EmbeddingGemma 2, Gemma 4).
· SQLite + sqlite-vec for vector storage.
· Android CLI for skill management.
· Claude Code / Codex / Gemini as build agents.
· Google Play Services Auth (play-services-auth:21.3.0) for optional sign-in.
· MCP over stdio or localhost HTTP.

3.3.4 Communication Interfaces

· None required for core function.
· Optional localhost WebSocket to a desktop MCP host.
· Optional HTTPS to backend for OAuth server auth code exchange.

3.4 Design Constraints

Per IEEE 29148, design constraints limit implementation choices :

ID Constraint
DC-1 Architecture shall use Kotlin + Jetpack Compose (Material 3).
DC-2 Build shall use Gradle KTS with version catalog.
DC-3 Modules shall be: :app, :core:capture, :core:embed, :core:memory, :core:llm, :core:mcp, :core:identity, :core:security, :core:validate.
DC-4 EmbeddingGemma 2 shall be the retrieval model.
DC-5 Gemma 4 E2B/E4B shall be the generation model via LiteRT-LM.
DC-6 Memory graph shall use SQLite + sqlite-vec with WAL mode.

